Copyright: Copyright: Copyright (C) 2026 The BeitDina Team (https://github.com/beitdina/nabataean-aramic\n\nSamaritan-Aramaic Font with Early Imperial Aramaic artistic influences from Petra. (cca. 920-270 BCE). \n\nNabataean-Aramaic Font with Proto-Sianitic and Nabataean-Aramaic artistic influences from Sinai, Syria and Israel..\n\nOfficial Aramaic Font of writing around 330-260 BCE preserved in Israel and Levanon, with Official Aramaic artistic influences. \n\nAncient Aramaic Font with Ancient Aramaic artistic influences (cca. 700-550 BCE) \n\nImperial Aramaic Font with Early Imperial Aramaic artistic influences (cca. 950-650 BCE)\n\nCreated with FontForge 20230101 at Fri Jul 24 05:03:14 2026 by Florin Ciprian Bodin aka orynider @ github.com/beitdina/early-aramaic original based on Cardo with SIL Open Font License, \nand some glyphs based on Noto Imperial Aramaic and Noto Samaritan made by The Not Noto Project Authors (https://github.com/notofonts/imperial-aramaic)\nand some portions of font metrics are based on GNU-GPL version and MIT License of Keter Aram Tzova by Yoram Knat \nwho used Hebrew OpenType Layout logic copyright (c) 2003 & 2007, Ralph Hancock & John Hudson. \nThis layout logic for Biblical Hebrew is open source software under the MIT License; for details  contact copyright holders at <license@tiro.com>, \nSome syriac glyphs are under Copyright 2022 by The Noto Project Authors (https://github.com/notofonts/syriac)
